{ dg-modules "genietransput" }
{ Rosetta Code, task "Loop over multiple arrays simultaneously", ALGOL 68 solution loop-over-multiple-arrays-simultaneously.alg.
  https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Loop_over_multiple_arrays_simultaneously#ALGOL_68
  The text of Rosetta Code is available under the GNU Free Documentation
  License 1.3 (see README.md).  The solution is unchanged in orig/loop-over-multiple-arrays-simultaneously.a68;
  this copy was prepared for ga68 and converted to SUPPER stropping by
  tools/rosetta_prep.py. }
access Genie_Transput (
[]union(char,int) x=("a","b","c"), y=("A","B","C"),
z=(1,2,3);
for i to UPB x do
  printf(($ggd$, x[i], y[i], z[i], $l$))
od
)
